  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nAbove average temperatures will remain through the week as an\nupper-level ridge persists over the Great Basin. Dry conditions,\nmostly clear skies, and temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above \nnormal are expected through the mid-week. Upper- level \ntroughing in the Gulf of Alaska will remain offshore until late \nThursday when the ridge moves east and weakens. Come Friday, \nmodels agree on the eastward movement of the strong longwave \ntrough offshore, but not on how far inland. This will be the\nleading difference in what the weather could be next weekend,\nwith possibilties ranging from widespread precipitation to none\nat all. For now, Friday and Saturday will see slight chances of\nrain / mountain snow and the beginning of a slight cooldown.",
